  "id": "COMPOUND:16821 - PROTEIN:6335",
  "verbalization": "Gallomyrtucommulone D appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7 (MRP7). The first pathway connects Gallomyrtucommulone D to Annexin A1, which is targeted by Excisusin B, and Excisusin B in turn targets MRP7. The second pathway links Gallomyrtucommulone D to Alpha-hemoglobin-stabilizing protein, which is targeted by a cyclohexanone compound, and this cyclohexanone compound also targets MRP7. Both pathways converge on MRP7 through distinct intermediates, suggesting that Gallomyrtucommulone D may exert its effects via different mechanisms that ultimately result in MRP7 being targeted. The evidence supports a potential role for Gallomyrtucommulone D in modulating MRP7 activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
